{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Before you took [Eb]your first breath, before [Bb]you knew [Eb]the land
The One who [Bb]made you, [F]Jacob, held [Gm]you in [Eb]his hand
The One [Bb]who formed you, Is[F]rael, will not let [Gm]go of [Eb]you
He gave E[Bb]gypt for your [F]ransom, Cush and Se[Bb]ba [Gm]too
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Do not [Bb]be af[Eb]raid, for I have [Bb]redeemed [F/A][Gm]you
I have [Eb]called you by name; [F]you are mine
[Gm]When you pass through [Bb]the wa[Eb]ters, I will be with [Bb][F/A]you
I [Gm]have called you [Eb]by [F]name; you are [Bb]mine
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
When the rivers rise around you and [Eb]the current pulls you [Bb]down
They [Eb]will not sweep you a[Bb]way, [F]you will [Gm]not drown
[Eb]When you walk through [Bb]fire, you [F]will not be [Gm]burned
[Eb]The flames will [Bb]not consume you, [F]he is with you every [Bb]turn
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Gm]Do not be [Bb]afraid, [Eb]for I have re[Bb]deemed [F/A]you
I [Gm]have called you [Eb]by name; you are [F]mine
When [Gm]you pass through the [Bb]waters, [Eb]I will be with [Bb]you
